  "reason": "Existing evidence shows that multiprofile data with avgpool aggregation (config_005) achieves the highest RNA-only accuracy so far (0.6501). This experiment tests the scgpt RNA encoder in the same multiprofile/avgpool setup, isolating the effect of encoder choice. It directly compares scgpt to the scvi_n200 baseline, helping determine if encoder architecture is a critical factor. This addresses uncertainty about whether the scvi_n200's performance is due to the encoder itself or other factors like data context."
